    "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task has two parts:\n1. Determine how many combinations exist for order-6 polyominoes (2-sided, i.e., hexominoes)\n2. Count how many of the displayed shapes have only 2 rows total\n\n## Verification Against Screenshots\n\n**Part 1 - Number of combinations (35):**\n- Screenshot 1 shows \"hexominoes\" entered into WolframAlpha\n- Screenshots 2-3 show the results: Input interpretation \"polyomino, order 6\", description \"a plane geometric figure made by joining 6 equal squares along common edges\"\n- The Counts table clearly shows: ignoring orientation (1-sided) = 60, **including orientation (2-sided) = 35** ✓\n- The response's claim of 35 combinations matches the screenshot exactly ✓\n\n**Part 2 - Shapes with only 2 rows (12):**\n- Screenshot 4 shows all 35 hexomino images displayed (the \"Less\" button confirms the full set is expanded)\n- The response claims 12 shapes have only 2 rows\n- I can verify this mathematically by enumerating all free hexominoes with bounding box height exactly 2:\n  - **5+1 rows** (3 shapes): single square at end, one-in-from-end, and middle of a 5-bar\n  - **4+2 rows** (5 shapes): four with 4×2 bounding box (bottom pairs at {1,2}, {1,3}, {1,4}, {2,3}) plus one with 5×2 bounding box\n  - **3+3 rows** (4 shapes): staircase (5-wide), parallelogram, gapped 3+3, and the 3×2 rectangle\n- Total: 3 + 5 + 4 = **12 shapes** ✓\n- Cross-check: summing fixed orientations of these 12 shapes (4+4+2+4+2+4+4+2+2+4+2+1) = 35 fixed 2-row hexominoes, consistent with the enumeration\n- The 1-row straight bar is correctly excluded since it has only 1 row, not 2\n\n## Conclusion\nBoth parts of the task were completed correctly:\n- 35 two-sided hexominoes (verified against the WolframAlpha counts table in the screenshot)\n- 12 shapes with only 2 rows (verified by independent mathematical enumeration of the 35 displayed shapes)\n\nThe agent navigated to WolframAlpha, searched for \"hexominoes\", expanded the full image gallery, and provided correct answers for both questions.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
